    "result_text": "Build succeeds and the test passes (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `sharesHousehold` / `householdId` feature for `POST /api/owners` in this OfficeFloor-based PetClinic.\n\nThe `sharesHousehold` request flag and the `EnsureUniqueOwnerHousehold` guard already existed (a matching lastName + address is rejected 409 unless `sharesHousehold` is true). What was missing was assigning and returning the shared `householdId`. I added:\n\n1. **`AssignOwnerHousehold`** (new function class) \u2014 runs after `BuildOwner`, before `SaveOwner`. It finds existing owners sharing the same normalized last name + address. If any exist (only reachable when `sharesHousehold` admitted the request), it assigns a **deterministic** 12-char hex identifier derived from the normalized household key (SHA-256), sets it on the new owner, and back-fills any existing members that lack one. A solo owner keeps `householdId` null.\n   - Deterministic derivation makes the id \"stable\" and shared regardless of creation order \u2014 the two joiners in the test resolve to the same value.\n\n2. **Pipeline wiring** \u2014 added the `assignHousehold` step to `owners.POST.yml` (under `transaction` governance, like its neighbors).\n\n3. **`householdId` field** on the `Owner` entity (`household_id` column) plus the column in all four DB schemas (hsqldb/h2/mysql/postgres).\n\n4. **openapi.yml** \u2014 added the read-only `householdId` property to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it (MapStruct maps it by name) and it's returned by `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreJoinersShareHouseholdId` (two `sharesHousehold` joiners share a non-blank `householdId`) passes, and the full suite is green.",
